WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.863
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.163 --> 00:00:08.050
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:13.881
Unit one: First Impressions. In this unit, you will talk about people and the impressions they make.

4
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:16.140
first impression.

5
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.813
first impression means the opinion you form when you meet someone for the first time.

6
00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:24.181
Nita made a great first impression at her job interview.

7
00:00:24.881 --> 00:00:27.510
Your turn. Say: first impression.

8
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.524
first impression.

9
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:33.425
approachable.

10
00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:36.635
approachable means friendly and easy to talk to.

11
00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:41.361
Our new manager is very approachable, so everyone asks her for advice.

12
00:00:42.061 --> 00:00:44.180
Your turn. Say: approachable.

13
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.985
approachable.

14
00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:49.822
reserved.

15
00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:53.485
reserved means quiet; not showing your feelings easily.

16
00:00:53.785 --> 00:00:56.864
He seems reserved at first, but he is very funny when you know him.

17
00:00:57.564 --> 00:00:59.659
Your turn. Say: reserved.

18
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:03.221
reserved.

19
00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:05.253
eye contact.

20
00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:09.717
eye contact means looking directly at the eyes of the person you are talking to.

21
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.806
Good eye contact shows that you are confident and honest.

22
00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.775
Your turn. Say: eye contact.

23
00:01:18.475 --> 00:01:19.569
eye contact.

24
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.654
small talk.

25
00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:26.420
small talk means polite conversation about everyday topics, like the weather.

26
00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.705
At networking events, people usually start with small talk.

27
00:01:31.405 --> 00:01:33.965
Your turn. Say: small talk.

28
00:01:36.665 --> 00:01:37.793
small talk.

29
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:39.773
appearance.

30
00:01:40.473 --> 00:01:43.436
appearance means the way someone or something looks.

31
00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.107
You shouldn't judge people only by their appearance.

32
00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:49.308
Your turn. Say: appearance.

33
00:01:52.008 --> 00:01:53.033
appearance.

34
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:54.855
handshake.

35
00:01:55.555 --> 00:01:58.994
handshake means the act of shaking hands when you meet or agree.

36
00:01:59.294 --> 00:02:01.967
A firm handshake is common in business meetings.

37
00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.960
Your turn. Say: handshake.

38
00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.498
handshake.

39
00:02:09.483 --> 00:02:10.496
reputation.

40
00:02:11.196 --> 00:02:15.018
reputation means the opinion that people generally have about someone.

41
00:02:15.318 --> 00:02:18.328
The café has a great reputation for friendly service.

42
00:02:19.028 --> 00:02:21.413
Your turn. Say: reputation.

43
00:02:24.113 --> 00:02:25.335
reputation.

44
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.291
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:28.591 --> 00:02:31.381
Nita, how was your first day at the internship?

46
00:02:32.683 --> 00:02:38.099
It was great! Everyone was approachable, and my supervisor gave me a warm handshake.

47
00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:42.767
That's a good sign. What did you do to make a good first impression?

48
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:48.951
I made eye contact, smiled a lot and started some small talk about the weather.

49
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:53.692
Perfect. People are judging your attitude more than your appearance.

50
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:57.796
I'm working hard to build a good reputation there.

51
00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:02.859
Grammar focus: Present simple vs present continuous.

52
00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:06.064
Present simple is for habits, facts and states.

53
00:03:06.364 --> 00:03:09.780
Present continuous is for actions happening now or for a short time.

54
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.007
For example: She works in a bank, but today she is working from home.

55
00:03:14.307 --> 00:03:18.977
State verbs like know, like, think and believe are not usually used in the continuous form.

56
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:22.682
Now read and listen. The Seven-Second Rule.

57
00:03:22.982 --> 00:03:27.373
Psychologists say that people form a first impression in about seven seconds.

58
00:03:28.683 --> 00:03:32.645
In that short time, we notice someone's appearance, body movements and voice.

59
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.772
A warm smile and good eye contact usually make a person look approachable.

60
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:43.625
However, a reserved person is not always unfriendly; they may simply be shy.

61
00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:49.296
That is why a fair reputation takes much longer to build than a quick impression.

62
00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:53.062
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:53.362 --> 00:03:56.301
A person who is friendly and easy to talk to is blank.

64
00:03:56.601 --> 00:04:00.650
A, reserved. B, approachable. C, appearance.

65
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.870
The answer is B: approachable.

66
00:04:08.383 --> 00:04:11.300
Right now, Nita blank an email to her supervisor.

67
00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.510
A, writes. B, is writing. C, write.

68
00:04:18.517 --> 00:04:20.447
The answer is B: is writing.

69
00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.170
Good blank shows you are confident and honest.

70
00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.961
A, eye contact. B, reputation. C, small talk.

71
00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.903
The answer is A: eye contact.

72
00:04:35.417 --> 00:04:37.405
I blank he is a very kind person.

73
00:04:37.705 --> 00:04:40.441
A, am thinking. B, think. C, thinks.

74
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.403
The answer is B: think.

75
00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:51.960
According to the text, people form a first impression in about blank.

76
00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:56.819
A, seven minutes. B, seven seconds. C, seven days.

77
00:05:00.817 --> 00:05:03.060
The answer is B: seven seconds.

78
00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:08.189
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you do to make a good first impression?

79
00:05:13.489 --> 00:05:17.846
I always make eye contact, smile, and ask the other person a friendly question.

80
00:05:18.146 --> 00:05:19.634
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:25.404
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present simple vs present continuous.

82
00:05:25.704 --> 00:05:28.913
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

83
00:05:29.213 --> 00:05:35.119
Congratulations! You have finished Online Intermediate. See you in Online Upper-Intermediate!

84
00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:38.211
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

